yzed by the msc phenotyping kit  showing a high expression of cd 73  90 and 105 the non-msc markers are  negative  and which is also a nice feature that  the hladr antibody which is  in most cases also a negative negatively  expressed on the cells can be analyzed  with a separate color here and this is  quite important because sometimes mses  are stimulated  like you can see here so the stimulation  can be done  by antiphon gamma or tnf alpha  to have a look of the  msc function in more detail but  sometimes it's also  the case when for example in fcs  containing media  a high amount of interference gamma is  present  then sometimes the hladr signal is quite  high  so therefore it's really nice to have  this marker  with a separate color here in this kit  to analyze it separately from the other  non-msc markers  because as you see here before  stimulation it's negative and after  stimulation with interferon gamma and  tnf alpha the signal is  quite high  the hybridoma antibodies  are quite an old technology  they were used in the old antibody kits  so this technology is from 1970  antibodies are produced as a hybridoma  in mouth and then later on in the  hybridoma cell culture  so the new way to produce  antibodies in a recombinant way  using here our affinity antibodies  is based on a system of a mammalian cell  production system  producing recombinant antibodies  antibodies  consisting partly of a human  and a mouse part  and there you have some benefits of  these rare affinity antibodies for  standard analysis  so first they are recommend generated  and they have one universal igg-1  isotype that improves of course  the reproducibility of  the essays in the lab later on  furthermore there is a mutation  a mutated fc region and this  improves or reduces the background  signal  so summing up these the kit is quite  easy to use  the five chiral antibody cocktail  includes three positive and five  negative antibodies for msc phenotyping  in addition an isotype control cocktail  and six individual antibodies for  compensation control  are also included  the assay is very standardized because  antibodies are included  that are defined by the isct consortium  for msc characterization by flow  cytometry  there is a really high lot to lot  consistency and repeat rebut  reproducibility because all the used  antibodies are reaffinity recombinant  antibodies  the kit is very reliable  because we use different flowchromes  for the hladr antibody to distinguish  between activated and non-activated mscs  i would like to come up now to the next  topic so which is sorting  mscs via the max quantity  so sorting cells bear  several problems so for example when you  sort cells with a cell sorter there's  high pressure and  shear stress affecting the viability and  function of cells  decontamination cleaning of fluidics  required after each run  there is a high chance of carry over  between different runs  and even when you are when we are  talking here about these  rare cells carry over is quite an  important topic  adjustment of drop delay and laser  alignment is needed  so the decompression of cells affect  viability and the functionality  application of charge affects viability  and function and might of  and might alter gene expression  safety concerns due to aerosol forming  or alternatively working under huge  biosafety cabinets  contamination of the sample affects  downstream processing so all these  these points are quite problematic and  therefore we have now the max quantity  it's with its unique features so it's  really gentle  to the cells because it has very low  pressure  no decompression enables resorting of  functional cells  and we have no cellulose in tubing sets  because the whole procedure takes place  in the cartridge and the  all cells are remaining in this  cartridge  the max quantity is fully sterile so  cartridge provides a closed system  so the cartridge system also  [Music]  gives some opportunity not to have any  carry over from  experiment to experiments because you  need  and use a separate cartridge for each  experiment  and do we do not have any contamination  of fluidics  so it's fully safe system the absence of  aerosol and droplets  and no biosafety cabinet is needed  the device is really easy to use so it's  a benchtop device no adjustment  of drop delay or laser alignment needed  and no cleaning required  so this cell sorting process here at the  title is  shown in more detail in this picture so  you really have  yeah no pressure no charge  less aerosol or no aerosol  development so at the end cells are  quite feeling well are very viable and  not activated in any  kind of process within here  so for the mscs we have done several  experiments  to use this device the max quantitative  for sorting using cd 271 and anti-msci1  as  specific markers expressed  on mscs coming from bone marrow  so we used bone marrow mononuclear cell  fraction  labeled with cd 271 pe  and anti-msca1 apc  [Music]  and you can see here before separation  there's  this is a really really low um  frequent cell population with only 0.04  percent  and after separation um there's a really  really high enrichment of cells  of more than ninety percent  also the viability is quite nice and if  you then  put these cells after sorting and also  compared to the situation before sorting  in culture you can  see that there's a high increase in  clonogenic potential  in these sorted cell population  here we analyzed the ability of cells  to expand and proliferate after the  sorting  process we have  passaged the cells several times and we  can  show here that the sorted cells grow in  a  comparable manner but like the plastic  appearance cells  also the marker expression is as it is  as it should be for mscs and also here  we looked for the t cell suppression  suppression potential so it's quite  preserved and comparable  before and after sorting  but besides sorting of course the  cultivation process is st